<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Antirrhinum majus Turing ocellus wavelength at 259 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 88.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 of the 259.13 µm ocellus (Holocene, 0 Ma). The radial power spectrum is now binned in physical wavenumber. At unit diffusivity the readback is 255.1 µm against λ_c = 259.13 µm (1.6% relative, was about 7% on integer pixel bins). The diffusivity sweep Pearson r is 0.99973 and RMSE(k) is 0.000263 µm⁻¹. Equal-diffusion σ_max stays −0.25 h⁻¹. Gallery pitch remains 77.8 µm (KS = 1 against the simulated gaps). The corner in σ(k) is marked as the unstable-band edge. GIF 800×600, 12 frames, CV similarity 83.6. Overall 88.1. No second assessor (R2). Overall 88.1/100 (faithfulness 87.6, reproducibility 89.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 3276935 B, 800×600 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 7ec4b0240db6d0c7bc707e1b06094421d59e6b3f85858e4a8f3daf5ebe4792bd (sha256 7ec4b0240db6d0c7bc707e1b06094421d59e6b3f85858e4a8f3daf5ebe4792bd), spec_fingerprint 9aa96d9174bbc264f2f19508483526998fd8a90a8bb5b00ee7c2a039134c8ca4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9aa96d9174bbc264f2f19508483526998fd8a90a8bb5b00ee7c2a039134c8ca4; artifact_sha256: 7ec4b0240db6d0c7bc707e1b06094421d59e6b3f85858e4a8f3daf5ebe4792bd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0/antirrhinum_majus_sete_cc-by-sa.jpg=4d2cd99ca49de264..., datasets/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=0918abca4751ad6b..., datasets/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=f3e9bf78a4453bc1...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Shang et al. 2010: Venosa MYB places anthocyanin over veins. | Noda et al. 1994: MIXTA conical epidermal cells intensify petal colour. | Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u=640, D_v=4341 µm²/h so that argmax σ(k) is 259.13 µm. | Physical-k radial bins and the annotated band edge.; transfer_boundary: Vein-locked Venosa pigment is not shown here to be a Turing instability. | The gallery pitch of 77.8 µm is a measurement of that asset.; does_not_claim: That Antirrhinum uses these kinetic constants in vivo. | That the gallery pitch equals 259.13 µm.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Closed in Pass 2. Physical-k bins. Unit-scale readback 255.1 µm vs 259.13 µm (1.6%).', 'status': 'closed'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Open. Single assessor; no second provider has scored this script.', 'status': 'open'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Closed in Pass 2. The dispersion panel marks the σ=0 crossing as the band edge.', 'status': 'closed'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.81e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

